d to spice  things up because kids these days need  more brain stimulation and a fast-paced  environment when it comes to watching  cartoons but it's not just the actual  show it's also the characters in it the  strong and funny characters from the  loud house are just absolutely perfect  and can make you laugh just as much as  the Peanuts characters can if you think  about it the loud house does indeed have  that relaxed Sunday feel to the show so  the team behind it definitely succeeded  in their mission rocky and bullwinkle  unless you're into old-school 60s  cartoons you  we have no idea who rocky and bullwinkle  are rocky and his friends is one of the  most progressive and absolutely  hilarious 1960 shows that still is  beloved to this day the series focuses  on The Adventures of a flying squirrel  called rocky and a slightly dim witted  moose named Bullwinkle this show was so  successful it also featured a series  called rocky and his friends as of 2018  the series has actually been revived on  Amazon and it's featuring a popular  cartoon voice actress Tara Strong but  you can frequently find the names Rocky  and Bullwinkle mentioned in pop culture  it was a show that Chris Savino grew up  watching as a child although he didn't  understand that cartoon making could  actually be a real-life job Rocky and  Bullwinkle along with several other  cartoon characters and shows we'll talk  about in a moment actually later  inspired Chris into the world of  animation you can also find a minor  Rocky and Bullwinkle reference in the  loud house episode called come sail away  the moose hockey player toy actually  resembles Bullwinkle Popeye speaking of  shows that Chris Savino watched when he  was a child  Popeye was also one of them who could  possibly forget about this spinach  eating character that managed to become  one of the most iconic cartoon  characters ever Popeye was also a show  that was frequently present in Chris  savino's life and he did mention it as  one o