ired by  Nickelodeon cartoon such as spongebob  Chris Savino actually managed to get his  first job on the Ren &amp; Stimpy show in  case you're not familiar with it the Ren  &amp; Stimpy show is a popular 90s cartoon  and one of the first original  Nickelodeon shows the series focuses on  The Adventures of the main characters  Rin and emotionally unstable Chihuahua  and Stimpy a happy-go-lucky cat it was  by far one of the most popular cartoons  if you grew up in the 90s but did you  know that Chris Savino was actually  responsible for the layout of Ren &amp;  Stimpy  and although Ren and Stimpy references  aren't present in the LAT house as of  yet you can find plenty of fan fictions  as well as fan art of the two worlds  colliding we can definitely see how the  crazy story lines and the defined  characters of the loud house would  connect with this iconic Ren &amp; Stimpy  show  Rocko's Modern Life we can also thank  Rocko's Modern Life for inspiring the  loud house Chris Savino had some pretty  impressive projects under his belt  before he created his own show and  Rocko's Modern Life is one of them you  can definitely tell that the loud house  wasn't just a one-hit wonder and the  animation process took a long time to  develop Chris was actually the creator  and prop designer from season 1 to  season 3 so you can actually thanked him  for creating such awesome and quirky  characters we're pretty sure we'd get  inspired by Rocko and wants to create  more exciting things after working on  such an awesome show in fact even some  of the show's comedic elements like  innuendos can be compared to the loud  house you can actually find the two  worlds merging in plenty of fan art and  fan fictions fans have actually plenty  of requests for the loud house  crossovers but Nickelodeon shows like  Rocko's Modern Life are probably the  most popular if you think about it it  wouldn't be that hard to bring the two  together considering they both come from  Nickelodeon Dexter's Laboratory  you probably remember Dexter the child  genius working in his laboratory while  his sister DeeDee tried to ruin  everything he ever worked on christina  was responsible for creating the  storyboard for season 3 and season 4 of  Dexter's Laboratory and while many  people didn't seem to enjoy those  particular seasons it's safe to say that  Dexter inspired the loud house have you  ever noticed the similarities between  Dexter and Lisa both are child geniuses  always working in the lab and absolutely  no one else in the family understands  what they're doing in fact they also  kind of look similar both never really  smile they're both short they're  insanely smart kind of crazy and they  almost have the same type of glasses  when Lisa is in her lab clothes she  definitely looks like Dexter fans of  Dexter's Laboratory have been comparing  Dexter and Lisa since the launch of the  loud house and you can definitely see  some similarities we can definitely  imagine Lisa as the female version of  Dexter especially since Chris Savino  actually worked on Dexter's Laboratory  we can't blame the fans wanting to see  this crossover seeing Lisa and Dexter  together would be adorable the Powerpuff  Girls here's another surprise you  probably didn't know unless you  religiously follow the world of animated  cartoons did you know that Chris Savino  worked on several episodes from multiple  seasons of one of the most beloved 90  shows the Powerpuff Girls he was the  director and story boarder which means  he was pretty much in charge of the  whole thing while fans of animated  cartoons weren't exactly impressed with  the execution of these two seasons it's  safe to say that the Powerpuff Girls did  serve as an inspiration for the lab  house the show is extremely colorful and  the colors even represent each of the  characters personalities considering  most of the loud house characters come  with a typical look and the same strong  and sometimes crazy personalities it's  safe to say Chris used the same concept  when he decided to create the loud house  and besides who knows if nickelodeon  would ever even approve of the loud  house without seeing chris's previous  work on all these Cartoon Network and  Nickelodeon shows unfortunately you  can't find any of the Powerpuff Girls  references on the loud house just yet to  keep your eyes peeled in the possible  future for shout outs because we have a  feeling they will happen newspaper  comics although they didn't start off as  TV shows many newspaper comics became  extremely successful shows  entered the world of animation in fact  some of the most iconic comic books  frequently get revived rebooted and  turned into actual cartoons Chris Savino  is never shy to mention that he owes his  animation career to newspaper comics  we've seen the connections without house  has with peanuts and Charlie Brown and  these are the comics and shows Kristen  joined as a child but it's not just  peanuts if you've paid attention to some  of the details in the loud house you'll  notice that the show also pays a tribute  to a comic called ctrl + Alt + delete  which is responsible for creating one of  the longest memes on the internet pay  attention to Lunas room and you'll  notice a poster on the top right corner  of the walls it's an extremely  simplified version of the popular  control-alt-delete comic called las  Chris Savino also frequently mentioned  how much he'd absolutely loved to own  his own comic book strip and who knows  maybe that'll be his next adventure and  his comic will be turned into a popular  show and that's all for our video do you  like the loud house let us know in the  comments thanks for watching see you  next time  [Music]

